

Here is the complete roadmap from beginner → advanced, with the most important LeetCode problems and the common thing you should remember.

🔥 TWO POINTER — COMPLETE PATTERN ROADMAP
Pattern 1: Opposite Direction — Left + Right
Idea

Two pointers start from opposite ends:

left →             ← right
[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]

Move one pointer depending on the condition.

Basic template
int left = 0;
int right = nums.length - 1;

while (left < right) {

    if (condition) {
        left++;
    } else {
        right--;
    }
}
Common problems
Reverse String — LeetCode 344
Valid Palindrome — LeetCode 125
Two Sum II — LeetCode 167
Container With Most Water — LeetCode 11
Boats to Save People — LeetCode 881==
Squares of a Sorted Array — LeetCode 977
🧠 Remember

Sorted array + find pair → think Left + Right.

For Two Sum II:

sum < target → left++
sum > target → right--
sum == target → answer


