Pattern 2: Slow + Fast Pointer

Both pointers move in the same direction.

slow →
fast →→

Usually used to modify/filter an array in-place.

Basic template
int slow = 0;

for (int fast = 0; fast < nums.length; fast++) {

    if (condition) {
        nums[slow] = nums[fast];
        slow++;
    }
}
Common problems
Remove Element — LeetCode 27
Remove Duplicates from Sorted Array — LeetCode 26
Move Zeroes — LeetCode 283
Remove Duplicates II — LeetCode 80
String Compression — LeetCode 443====
🧠 Remember

One pointer searches, one pointer stores.

fast = scans
slow = stores

This is extremely important.
