Intersection of Two Arrays — LeetCode 349
🧠 Remember

Two sorted arrays → one pointer for each array.

Pattern 8: Two Pointer for Palindrome

This is actually a special case of opposite-direction pointers.

left →         ← right

a b c d c b a
↑             ↑

Compare:

while (left < right) {

    if (s.charAt(left) != s.charAt(right)) {
        return false;
    }

    left++;
    right--;
}
Problems
Valid Palindrome — LC 125
Valid Palindrome II — LC 680
Palindrome Linked List — LC 234
🧠 Remember

Compare beginning and ending → Left + Right.
